Thinks you could do good
at the US Amateur.

492
00:27:58.512 --> 00:27:59.804
said there could be some money in it.

493
00:27:59.805 --> 00:28:01.931
I already told him.
"I'm not interested. man."

494
00:28:01.932 --> 00:28:06.269
I told him that.
So. I just wanna be alone right now. okay?

495
00:28:06.270 --> 00:28:07.688
No. I wanna talk about this.

496
00:28:08.355 --> 00:28:09.981
I'm worried about you.

497
00:28:09.982 --> 00:28:13.819
I haven't seen you happy in a long time.
and I just think this is something that...

498
00:28:14.486 --> 00:28:16.863
- That you should think about.
- I'm fucking done with golf.

499
00:28:16.864 --> 00:28:19.991
- <i>Mami</i>. I'm not doing that again.
- Okay. don't use that tone with me.

500
00:28:19.992 --> 00:28:22.326
I mean. why would you want me
to play again after what happened?

501
00:28:22.327 --> 00:28:25.622
Because the last time I saw you smile
was on a golf course.

502
00:28:26.373 --> 00:28:29.000
- Geez.
- I know what it means to you.

503
00:28:29.001 --> 00:28:30.960
Golf used to make you happy.

504
00:28:30.961 --> 00:28:32.503
Well. he ruined it for me.

505
00:28:32.504 --> 00:28:36.466
No. golf doesn't have to be what it was
before when your dad was here.

506
00:28:38.260 --> 00:28:40.387
It can be whatever you want it to be.

507
00:28:44.474 --> 00:28:47.727
Well. go and find out
how serious this guy is.

508
00:28:47.728 --> 00:28:50.229
Okay.

509
00:28:50.230 --> 00:28:51.773
Yeah. Yeah.

510
00:29:04.620 --> 00:29:05.829
Hi.

511
00:29:08.290 --> 00:29:10.041
- Uh-oh.
- Sorry. they're loud but they don't bite.

512
00:29:10.042 --> 00:29:11.376
Okay.

513
00:29:11.960 --> 00:29:14.545
- Welcome.
- Thanks for meeting me.

514
00:29:14.546 --> 00:29:17.049
Glad there's some openness to the idea.

515
00:29:21.428 --> 00:29:22.846
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

516
00:29:23.597 --> 00:29:26.015
And before we get started.
let me just say again.

517
00:29:26.016 --> 00:29:30.228
I could not believe any more strongly
in your son's talent.

518
00:29:30.229 --> 00:29:31.938
You did a great job.

519
00:29:31.939 --> 00:29:33.023
Thank you.

520
00:29:35.484 --> 00:29:37.069
I saw your YouTube clip.

521
00:29:38.987 --> 00:29:41.155
- Yeah.
- And?

522
00:29:41.156 --> 00:29:42.699
Did you ever play again after that?

523
00:29:45.786 --> 00:29:46.911
No. not really.

524
00:29:46.912 --> 00:29:49.331
It was kinda hard to come back
from something like that.

525
00:29:50.165 --> 00:29:51.333
And what happened?

526
00:29:54.753 --> 00:29:55.838
Life.

527
00:29:58.757 --> 00:29:59.758
Yeah.

528
00:30:00.843 --> 00:30:03.177
- Okay. here's the deal.
- Let's hear it.

529
00:30:03.178 --> 00:30:06.055
- You pay for travel. for both of us.
- Okay. For both?

530
00:30:06.056 --> 00:30:07.640
Both.

531
00:30:07.641 --> 00:30:10.017
You cover all entry fees.
All the equipment.

532
00:30:10.018 --> 00:30:11.310
Okay.

533
00:30:11.311 --> 00:30:12.478
And if this works out.

534
00:30:12.479 --> 00:30:15.398
and if I know anything. the smart money
is on this not working out.

535
00:30:15.399 --> 00:30:17.066
You never know.

536
00:30:17.067 --> 00:30:19.610
But if it works out. we would go 70-30.

537
00:30:19.611 --> 00:30:22.573
- 70-30?
- On everything he makes.

538
00:30:25.659 --> 00:30:27.493
- Deal. I agree.
- Okay.

539
00:30:27.494 --> 00:30:29.371
And you pay me $100.000.

540
00:30:30.831 --> 00:30:33.333
Okay. you want that in crypto
or gold bullion?

541
00:30:33.917 --> 00:30:35.836
No. I think cash. Cash is good.

542
00:30:36.378 --> 00:30:38.630
And that would be before we hit the road.

543
00:30:40.007 --> 00:30:42.508
I thought you were kidding.
Are you serious?

544
00:30:42.509 --> 00:30:45.428
I mean. do I look like I have a spare 100K
laying around?

545
00:30:45.429 --> 00:30:49.599
You were just saying the smart money's
on it not working out. and--

546
00:30:49.600 --> 00:30:52.018
Well. yeah. and you were just saying
that you couldn't believe in him more.

547
00:30:52.019 --> 00:30:53.311
- So...
- That's true.

548
00:30:53.312 --> 00:30:55.271
I... It's just...

549
00:30:55.272 --> 00:30:57.106
That's a lot of money.

550
00:30:57.107 --> 00:30:59.942
Look. I just know how good my son is.

551
00:30:59.943 --> 00:31:01.570
I mean...

552
00:31:02.362 --> 00:31:03.405
Come.

553
00:31:03.989 --> 00:31:08.619
He stopped playing when he was 14.
but before that. he won everything.

554
00:31:09.244 --> 00:31:12.288
Okay. and I have two more boxes over there
in the garage full like this.

555
00:31:12.289 --> 00:31:14.290
- He won all these?
- He wins everything.

556
00:31:14.291 --> 00:31:16.250
All the time. Everything.

557
00:31:16.251 --> 00:31:18.211
I have our future to think about.

558
00:31:18.212 --> 00:31:20.129
I can't go on some wild goose chase.

559
00:31:20.130 --> 00:31:21.590
No.

560
00:31:24.593 --> 00:31:25.843
Who coached him?

561
00:31:25.844 --> 00:31:27.512
His dad.

562
00:31:27.513 --> 00:31:29.263
He did a good job.

563
00:31:29.264 --> 00:31:30.974
Why'd he stop playing?

564
00:31:32.142 --> 00:31:33.310
His dad.

565
00:31:34.436 --> 00:31:36.104
Where's his dad now?

566
00:31:37.481 --> 00:31:38.982
If you find him. let me know.

567
00:31:41.610 --> 00:31:43.110
I'm just saying. it's a weak hustle.

568
00:31:43.111 --> 00:31:44.904
No. it's not a hustle.

569
00:31:44.905 --> 00:31:46.323
It's an opportunity.

570
00:31:47.115 --> 00:31:49.200
An opportunity to what? Lose 100 grand?

571
00:31:49.201 --> 00:31:51.202
I mean. you've got better odds
playing keno.

572
00:31:51.203 --> 00:31:52.621
That's not true.

573
00:31:53.205 --> 00:31:54.830
They just put more waffles out.

574
00:31:54.831 --> 00:31:56.207
I'm full. but there's waffles.

575
00:31:56.208 --> 00:31:58.876
- Why do you still do this?
- What are you talking about?

576
00:31:58.877 --> 00:32:02.881
You think I'm gonna let 287.000
DoubleTree points go to waste?

577
00:32:04.007 --> 00:32:05.883
Stop it. There's a whole buffet up there.

578
00:32:05.884 --> 00:32:07.844
- Get some of the fiesta ranchero sauce.
- Mitts. listen.

579
00:32:07.845 --> 00:32:09.054
Okay. Listen to me.

580
00:32:10.055 --> 00:32:12.057
If I don't do this. what am I gonna do?

581
00:32:12.683 --> 00:32:14.058
I didn't turn out.

582
00:32:14.059 --> 00:32:17.728
Let's be honest.
I've been spinning my wheels for years.

583
00:32:17.729 --> 00:32:20.023
And I am nowhere.

584
00:32:22.776 --> 00:32:23.901
Okay.

585
00:32:23.902 --> 00:32:26.822
You know. this kid's not gonna fix
what happened. right?

586
00:32:27.990 --> 00:32:29.156
I didn't say it would.

587
00:32:29.157 --> 00:32:30.616
I understand that.

588
00:32:30.617 --> 00:32:32.869
But maybe it's a chance
to leave something behind

589
00:32:32.870 --> 00:32:35.914
other than a YouTube clip
of the worst day of my life.

590
00:32:36.915 --> 00:32:38.165
Here's the thing.

591
00:32:38.166 --> 00:32:39.667
You know zero about this kid.

592
00:32:39.668 --> 00:32:43.296
Okay. fine. he can nuke it off the tee.
but you haven't even seen his whole game.

593
00:32:43.297 --> 00:32:46.549
- Mitts. I have a feeling. all right?
- Yeah.

594
00:32:46.550 --> 00:32:51.345
Look. this game. it takes
and it takes and it takes from me.

595
00:32:51.346 --> 00:32:55.183
Finally. the other day it taps me
on the shoulder. and I turn.

596
00:32:55.184 --> 00:32:58.269
"Now what? Now what are you
gonna strip away from me?"

597
00:32:58.270 --> 00:32:59.979
Only it didn't want anything.

598
00:32:59.980 --> 00:33:02.274
It actually had its hands out like this.

599
00:33:02.941 --> 00:33:05.527
Holding a beautiful blue Tiffany's box.

600
00:33:06.528 --> 00:33:09.489
And I take it. and I open it up.
and guess what's inside?

601
00:33:10.449 --> 00:33:11.824
The kid.

602
00:33:11.825 --> 00:33:14.036
The kid is in the box.

603
00:33:15.829 --> 00:33:17.622
Are you on mushrooms right now?

604
00:33:17.623 --> 00:33:19.499
No. I'm not on mushrooms.

605
00:33:20.083 --> 00:33:23.669
I'm saying the game
is finally giving me something back.

606
00:33:23.670 --> 00:33:25.171
And it's about time.

607
00:33:25.172 --> 00:33:27.006
Because it owes me.

608
00:33:27.007 --> 00:33:29.927
You were my caddy for 15 years.
it owes you too.

609
00:33:31.386 --> 00:33:32.721
Right?

610
00:33:33.972 --> 00:33:35.641
Where are you gonna get 100 grand?

611
00:33:36.808 --> 00:33:39.060
Mikey D. Pryce Cahill.

612
00:33:39.061 --> 00:33:40.269
How are you. amigo?

613
00:33:40.270 --> 00:33:43.147
Hey. I got a quick question for you.

614
00:33:43.148 --> 00:33:45.399
How would you like to get rich?

615
00:33:45.400 --> 00:33:47.860
Yes. $100.000 is a lot of money.

616
00:33:47.861 --> 00:33:50.488
But what would you say if we were getting
in on the ground floor

617
00:33:50.489 --> 00:33:51.949
of the next Tiger Woods?

618
00:33:52.491 --> 00:33:53.908
Hello. Steve?

619
00:33:53.909 --> 00:33:57.954
Carla. look. can I just say
one thing in my defense. please?

620
00:33:57.955 --> 00:34:03.251
This kid has more natural talent
than any golfer I've ever seen.

621
00:34:03.252 --> 00:34:05.378
It's a very simple plan. Doug.

622
00:34:05.379 --> 00:34:12.051
We take him on the road.
and we turn this kid into a gold mine.

623
00:34:12.052 --> 00:34:15.680
Listen. I fell off a Bird scooter. okay?

624
00:34:15.681 --> 00:34:17.430
That's why you hadn't heard from me.

625
00:34:17.431 --> 00:34:19.350
I know there are no sure things.

626
00:34:19.351 --> 00:34:21.395
Okay. well. then call it a loan if...

627
00:34:21.978 --> 00:34:22.980
Hello?

628
00:34:26.525 --> 00:34:27.860
Okay. come on.

629
00:34:28.485 --> 00:34:29.526
Let's go. Pryce.

630
00:34:29.527 --> 00:34:31.946
Put a little extra cash in your pocket.

631
00:34:31.947 --> 00:34:34.698
Spoil Rachel.
Maybe take her to the Bahamas.

632
00:34:34.699 --> 00:34:37.910
<i>Rachel and I broke up.
I'm living with my dad again.</i>

633
00:34:37.911 --> 00:34:39.453
Well. take him to the Bahamas.

634
00:34:39.454 --> 00:34:41.414
I'm sure I could still dial a phone.

635
00:34:41.415 --> 00:34:44.375
but it's hard if you've broken an arm
and you're depressed.

636
00:34:44.376 --> 00:34:45.834
I didn't wanna bring you down.

637
00:34:45.835 --> 00:34:48.421
And. Carla... Carla?

638
00:34:48.422 --> 00:34:50.256
It's not a boondoggle. believe me.

639
00:34:50.257 --> 00:34:52.758
I've spent my life on boondoggles.

640
00:34:52.759 --> 00:34:54.719
This is anything but a boondoggle.

641
00:34:55.804 --> 00:34:57.848
Come... Really?

642
00:35:03.312 --> 00:35:07.857
I don't know why someone would have
one bathroom with a four bedroom house.

643
00:35:07.858 --> 00:35:09.317
Can I call you right back

644
00:35:09.318 --> 00:35:13.404
because a Bible salesman
just walked into my office?

645
00:35:13.405 --> 00:35:14.781
Okay. thanks.

646
00:35:15.657 --> 00:35:16.782
Why are you wearing a tie?

647
00:35:16.783 --> 00:35:21.537
Because I'm here in an official capacity.
and I got a business proposition for you.

648
00:35:21.538 --> 00:35:22.663
What's this?

649
00:35:22.664 --> 00:35:25.250
The thing for the house. I signed it.

650
00:35:27.753 --> 00:35:29.712
So you're not gonna
be an asshole about it?

651
00:35:29.713 --> 00:35:31.255
No. not this time.

652
00:35:31.256 --> 00:35:33.257
So. what's the proposition?

653
00:35:33.258 --> 00:35:36.385
Well. you know how you said
you'd give me 75K if I signed it?

654
00:35:36.386 --> 00:35:38.430
- I need a little more.
- Hold on.

655
00:35:41.433 --> 00:35:42.808
I didn't wanna do a spit take.

656
00:35:42.809 --> 00:35:44.645
- How much?
- Hundred thousand.

657
00:35:46.271 --> 00:35:48.064
Why do you need $100.000?

658
00:35:48.065 --> 00:35:50.025
Fresh start. like you said.

659
00:35:50.651 --> 00:35:52.194
They're expensive these days.

660
00:35:55.906 --> 00:35:58.115
Yes? I'll take that as a yes.

661
00:35:58.116 --> 00:36:01.953
Come on. What is the angle. Pryce?
I can see this from a mile away.

662
00:36:01.954 --> 00:36:03.246
- What is it?
- No.

663
00:36:03.247 --> 00:36:07.124
I found a kid who swings a golf club
like a goddamn dream.

664
00:36:07.125 --> 00:36:08.793
I wanna take him on the road.

665
00:36:08.794 --> 00:36:11.087
You're stake horsing now.

666
00:36:11.088 --> 00:36:12.296
Smart.

667
00:36:12.297 --> 00:36:14.924
How much of our money have you lost
with your crazy fucking schemes?

668
00:36:14.925 --> 00:36:17.426
No. this isn't a scheme.
I wanna help this kid.

669
00:36:17.427 --> 00:36:18.970
I wanna teach him what I know.

670
00:36:18.971 --> 00:36:21.639
It's never about somebody else. Pryce.
It's always about you.

671
00:36:21.640 --> 00:36:23.140
Fine. let's say it's about me.

672
00:36:23.141 --> 00:36:25.309
But it's also about this kid.

673
00:36:25.310 --> 00:36:30.898
And you should see this kid
because he is great.

674
00:36:30.899 --> 00:36:32.860
No. It's not gonna happen.

675
00:36:33.735 --> 00:36:37.071
Come on. you said if I signed it.
you'd help me start over.

676
00:36:37.072 --> 00:36:41.158
Yeah. I thought it would be for
a down payment for a condo or something.

677
00:36:41.159 --> 00:36:44.245
I know. but this...
Come on. this is so much better than that.

678
00:36:44.246 --> 00:36:45.580
No. I'm not doing it.

679
00:36:45.581 --> 00:36:49.041
Honestly. I swear. if you saw this kid.
I think you would understand.

680
00:36:49.042 --> 00:36:51.961
- I don't have time for this.
- Let me show you how good he is.

681
00:36:51.962 --> 00:36:53.421
- No.
- Fifteen minutes.

682
00:36:53.422 --> 00:36:56.132
- I don't have 15 minutes.
- Well. let me prove it to you.

683
00:36:56.133 --> 00:36:57.758
- No. I'm not giving you 100 grand.
- Good.

684
00:36:57.759 --> 00:37:00.970
I don't want you to give it to me
unless you see what I see.

685
00:37:00.971 --> 00:37:02.180
I'm not giving it to you.

686
00:37:02.181 --> 00:37:03.931
And I'm going to be late
for a walk-through.

687
00:37:03.932 --> 00:37:06.059
Please. 15 minutes.

688
00:37:08.604 --> 00:37:10.980
- Hey. Rebecca. Is Santi back there?
- Yes. he is.

689
00:37:10.981 --> 00:37:12.191
Great.

690
00:37:13.609 --> 00:37:14.775
Santi. hey!

691
00:37:14.776 --> 00:37:17.320
- No. You cannot be here.
- No. I need you to come with me.

692
00:37:17.321 --> 00:37:19.572
- Just two minutes. That's it.
- You have no sense of boundaries.

693
00:37:19.573 --> 00:37:21.449
- I'm working. I can't--
- Please.

694
00:37:21.450 --> 00:37:23.201
Front parking lot. Just come with me.

695
00:37:23.202 --> 00:37:25.411
All I need you to do is swing a club.

696
00:37:25.412 --> 00:37:27.247
Maybe change your life forever.

697
00:37:28.749 --> 00:37:30.417
What? Wait.

698
00:37:31.210 --> 00:37:33.377
Hey. what are you doing
in my stock room again?

699
00:37:33.378 --> 00:37:34.587
He's in the middle of a shift.

700
00:37:34.588 --> 00:37:36.130
He's taking his break.

701
00:37:36.131 --> 00:37:37.381
You get a smoke break. right?

702
00:37:37.382 --> 00:37:39.884
Or whatever your generation needs.
Like a mental health time-out?

703
00:37:39.885 --> 00:37:42.053
- Listen. asshole. I don't know who you--
- Again with the cussing.

704
00:37:42.054 --> 00:37:43.430
It's just lazy.

705
00:37:45.432 --> 00:37:48.226
Santi. get back inside right now.

706
00:37:48.227 --> 00:37:50.603
Okay. Santi.
you see that lovely woman over there.

707
00:37:50.604 --> 00:37:52.563
That's Amber-Linn. my ex-wife.

708
00:37:52.564 --> 00:37:53.773
So sorry about him.

709
00:37:53.774 --> 00:37:55.316
I need you to show her how good you are.

710
00:37:55.317 --> 00:37:57.568
One shot. Over the parking lot.

711
00:37:57.569 --> 00:37:58.819
Through the trees

712
00:37:58.820 --> 00:38:01.155
and into that yellow dumpster
at the end of the alley.

713
00:38:01.156 --> 00:38:03.199
Okay. Santi. get back in the store.

714
00:38:03.200 --> 00:38:07.161
Santi. look. you do this.
and I can get you and your mom the money.

715
00:38:07.162 --> 00:38:10.206
You do this.
and you are off the manager track.

716
00:38:10.207 --> 00:38:13.626
Big deal. So you lose out
on being this jerk in five years?

717
00:38:13.627 --> 00:38:18.214
One shot. 175 yard baby draw.
through the gap in the trees.

718
00:38:18.215 --> 00:38:20.383
Stick it in that yellow dumpster.

719
00:38:20.384 --> 00:38:22.468
I told you. man.
I don't want to play golf anymore.

720
00:38:22.469 --> 00:38:24.470
And I don't believe you.

721
00:38:24.471 --> 00:38:28.350
Look. whatever happened to make you
stop playing this game. you gotta face it.

722
00:38:29.142 --> 00:38:32.395
Trust me. I know what it's like
to put your life on hold

723
00:38:32.396 --> 00:38:33.689
'cause something bad happened.

724
00:38:34.314 --> 00:38:35.940
I've been doing it for years.

725
00:38:35.941 --> 00:38:37.441
But you have a gift.

726
00:38:37.442 --> 00:38:39.735
Okay. you were put here to play this game.

727
00:38:39.736 --> 00:38:41.696
You and I both know that.

728
00:38:41.697 --> 00:38:43.824
Don't turn your back on that.

729
00:38:44.741 --> 00:38:45.826
Come on.

730
00:38:47.369 --> 00:38:49.996
You take this swing
and it is over. young man.

731
00:38:49.997 --> 00:38:52.624
No. you take this swing.
and it is just the beginning.

732
00:38:56.879 --> 00:38:59.089
- Let's go.
- Yes. come on.

733
00:39:00.299 --> 00:39:02.717
Okay. you're gonna wanna
open the club a little bit

734
00:39:02.718 --> 00:39:04.636
- to make it through those trees.
- I got it.

735
00:39:06.388 --> 00:39:07.847
Move it up just a little bit
in your stance.

736
00:39:07.848 --> 00:39:09.223
Yeah. I know what I'm doing.

737
00:39:09.224 --> 00:39:12.477
Hey. trust me.

738
00:39:51.600 --> 00:39:53.769
Yes! Come on!

739
00:40:10.327 --> 00:40:12.453
There's two qualifiers
before the US Amateurs

740
00:40:12.454 --> 00:40:14.914
and about a half dozen tournaments
in between.

741
00:40:14.915 --> 00:40:16.457
But amateurs can get paid now.

742
00:40:16.458 --> 00:40:20.211
Okay. this kid does well.
the sky's the limit.

743
00:40:20.212 --> 00:40:21.380
What do you think?

744
00:40:23.423 --> 00:40:26.926
I think that when you want something
you are unstoppable.

745
00:40:26.927 --> 00:40:29.512
- Yes.
- I had forgotten this side of you.

746
00:40:29.513 --> 00:40:31.098
Don't forget that side.

747
00:40:31.890 --> 00:40:33.100
You sure about this?

748
00:40:33.892 --> 00:40:37.145
You've been saying I need to move on.
Maybe this is my chance.

749
00:40:39.231 --> 00:40:40.566
It won't bring him back.

750
00:40:41.400 --> 00:40:42.484
I know.

751
00:40:52.953 --> 00:40:54.996
- <i>Hello.</i>
- Hey. it's Pryce.

752
00:40:54.997 --> 00:40:56.956
- I got the money.
- <i>What?</i>

753
00:40:56.957 --> 00:40:59.542
You got the $100.000?

754
00:40:59.543 --> 00:41:03.796
- Yep. We leave Saturday.
- This Saturday? I mean. so soon?

755
00:41:03.797 --> 00:41:06.133
We gotta get him ready
for the Amateur in August.

756
00:41:07.718 --> 00:41:08.886
Right.

757
00:41:10.387 --> 00:41:11.929
Okay.

758
00:41:11.930 --> 00:41:13.931
- Yeah. let's do it.
- <i>Here we go.</i>

759
00:41:13.932 --> 00:41:15.893
- Let's do it.
- All right. see you.

760
00:42:01.772 --> 00:42:02.773
Yes!

761
00:42:03.357 --> 00:42:04.941
<i>I'm pulling back.</i>

762
00:42:04.942 --> 00:42:06.944
First strawberry...

763
00:42:08.529 --> 00:42:10.488
Fondue. A little treat.

764
00:42:10.489 --> 00:42:12.281
All right. thank you.

765
00:42:12.282 --> 00:42:14.868
- There we go.
- Remember you... Ever...

766
00:42:18.413 --> 00:42:19.498
Hey.

767
00:42:22.543 --> 00:42:24.419
You're the one that took a nap.

768
00:42:25.963 --> 00:42:29.632
Ready for the Pryce Cahill hangover cure?

769
00:42:29.633 --> 00:42:33.845
<i>Well. I have the Pryce Cahill hangover so...</i>

770
00:42:33.846 --> 00:42:36.597
I feel like it's only fair.

771
00:42:36.598 --> 00:42:41.018
I wanna get your whole regimen
because you have such a beautiful smile.

772
00:42:41.019 --> 00:42:43.354
Anything to show us
other than a beautiful smile?

773
00:42:43.355 --> 00:42:44.939
No. nothing.

774
00:42:44.940 --> 00:42:47.483
- <i>Nothing?</i>
- <i>Nothing at all.</i>

775
00:42:47.484 --> 00:42:49.694
<i>What the heck?</i>

776
00:42:49.695 --> 00:42:51.737
We are getting close. aren't we?

777
00:42:51.738 --> 00:42:53.406
Sometimes you can do this test. Oh. yeah.

778
00:42:53.407 --> 00:42:56.534
- <i>It's like a melon.</i>
- <i>Three weeks. Three weeks.</i>

779
00:42:56.535 --> 00:42:58.287
- You think three?
- Yeah.

780
00:43:00.372 --> 00:43:01.497
Did it work?

781
00:43:01.498 --> 00:43:02.748
He's asleep?

782
00:43:02.749 --> 00:43:07.295
"No. Daddy. Stop filming me.
Stop filming me. Daddy."

783
00:43:07.296 --> 00:43:08.964
<i>Aw.</i>

784
00:43:10.716 --> 00:43:12.885
There you go. Look at you!

785
00:43:14.136 --> 00:43:15.053
No.

786
00:43:17.681 --> 00:43:20.516
I wanna play golf.

787
00:43:20.517 --> 00:43:22.810
<i>Here. you have this one.</i>

788
00:43:22.811 --> 00:43:24.478
Little grip.

789
00:43:24.479 --> 00:43:25.898
That one right there.

790
00:43:26.607 --> 00:43:27.691
I knew it!

791
00:43:28.901 --> 00:43:31.027
Ready. guys? Here we go.

792
00:43:31.028 --> 00:43:40.287
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

793
00:43:40.954 --> 00:43:45.209
<i>Happy birthday dear Jett!</i>

